Solve, algebraically.
\[
9^{2 x+3}=\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^{x+1}
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
\left(3^{2}\right)^{2 x+3} & =\left(3^{-1}\right)^{x+1} & & 1 \text { mark for changing to a common base } \\
3^{4 x+6} & =3^{-x-1} & & \\
4 x+6 & =-x-1 & & 1 \text { mark for equating exponents with a common base } \\
5 x & =-7 & & 2 \text { marks } \\
x & =-\frac{7}{5} & &
\end{aligned}
\]

