Solve, algebraically.
\[
\frac{5!(n-5)!}{3!(n-6)!}=80
\]

Solution
\[
\begin{aligned}
\frac{5 \cdot 4 \cdot 3!(n-5)(n-6)!}{3!(n-6)!} & =80 \\
20(n-5) & =80 \\
n-5 & =4 \\
n & =9
\end{aligned}
\]

1 mark for factorial expansion ( \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for each) \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for simplification of factorials
\(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for solving for \(n\)

